    "message": "Tricks: Powerloop's own window and Double Powerloop, Trippy at 360 deg / 150 deg/s, long tricks to 10 s; the owner's depot log as a fixture\n\nFrom the owner's ?tricks=debug log (90 attempts, Warehouse, bf core):\n\n- Powerloop: >= 300 deg of pitch inside its own 3.5 s window (LOOP_WIN_S),\n  not Flip's 1.2 s; after the top the path may end up to 1.5 m above the\n  entry (loopRet >= -1.5). Loops are counted over the segment's whole turn\n  of pitch: 600 deg is a Double Powerloop, then one per further 360 deg;\n  each loop scores the Powerloop's points and the pop names it.\n- Trippy: >= 360 deg about the vertical at >= 150 deg/s while the path\n  orbits >= 360 deg at 0.3-2.5 m; no roll term, so a rolling trippy counts.\n- Long tricks: a segment turning about the vertical at Trippy's rate, or\n  looping, runs past 4.5 s while it keeps turning, up to 10 s.\n- tools/fixtures/tricklog-depot-bf-1.jsonl.gz (the log, verbatim) and\n  tools/test_sim_tricks_attempt_log.mjs: seq 4/59/79 -> Powerloop (4, 59\n  Double), 22/23/24 -> Trippy, every fired label unchanged, the rest pinned\n  (25 -> Trippy, 75 -> Powerloop).\n- Overlay: gate copy, loop fields in its records, Double Powerloop name.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
